      "writtenOn": "2026-06-26T15:47:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The secrets don\u0027t have those attributes in it, the serialized secret has a slightly different form generated from that, but contains the connection and project information.  That is definitely larger than 128 bytes in the tests.  And is almost certain to be larger than 128 bytes for any real-world secret.\n\nI don\u0027t think we need to add an extra assertion, if the secrets grow to larger than 1024 bytes with the new mock.patch in place, then the test will fail (just as it does now without the mock.patch).",
